@file FLT/AutomorphicForm/QuaternionAlgebra/Basic.lean
@decl TotallyDefiniteQuaternionAlgebra.WeightTwoAutomorphicForm.LevelStruct.isFiniteRelIndex_Δ
-- L4DEL: title: `[Δ_g : Fˣ]` is finite
-- L4DEL: intuition: `[Δ_g : Fˣ]` is finite. Since `g⁻¹ U g` is compact open, `g⁻¹ U g ⊆ x⁻¹GL₂(∏ 𝒪_{Fᵥ})x` for some `x`. Let `𝒪 := x⁻¹M₂(∏ 𝒪_{Fᵥ})x ∩ D`. Then `𝒪` is an order (why?) and `Δ_g/Fˣ ↪ 𝒪¹ := { x ∈ 𝒪 | N(x) = 1 }`, where the latter is finite because it is discrete and bounded in `D ⊗_{ℚ} ℝ = ∏ ℍ` (See Lemma 17.7.13 in Voight).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

