@file FLT/AutomorphicForm/QuaternionAlgebra/HeckeOperators/Concrete.lean
@decl TotallyDefiniteQuaternionAlgebra.HeckeAlgebra
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: HeckeAlgebra
-- L4DEL: intuition: Given `𝒮 : U₁Data F R p`, `HeckeAlgebra D 𝒮` is the Hecke algebra associated to the weight 2 `R`-valued automorphic forms associated to the discriminant 1 totally definite quaternion algebra `D` over the totally real field `F`, of level `U₁(S, Q)` where `S` is a finite set of nonzero primes `v` of `𝓞 F`. To make sense of this definition we choose a rigidification, that is, a fixed `𝔸_F^∞`-linear isomorphism `D ⊗[F] 𝔸_F^∞ = M₂(𝔸_F^∞)`, enabling us to define level structures and Hecke operators `Tᵥ` and `Uᵥ` using 2x2 matrices. Details: `𝒮 : U₁Data F R p` consist of a set of bad primes `S` of `F` with order `p` characters `k(v) →* R`, and a set of taylor wiles primes `Q`. `U₁(S, Q)` is the subgroup of `(D ⊗[F] 𝔸_F^∞)ˣ` associated, via `r`, to the matrices which are in `GL₂(𝓞ᵥ)` for all `v ∉ S ∪ Q` and which are of the form `(* *; 0 *)` mod `v` for all `v ∈ S`, and `(a *; 0 d)` mod `v` with `p ∤ ord(a/d)` for `v ∈ Q`. The Hecke algebra is defined to be the sub-`R`-algebra of the weight 2 forms of level `U₁(S, Q)` generated by the following two kinds of Hecke operators: first there are the operators `Tᵥ` associated to the matrices `(ϖᵥ 0; 0 1)` for `v ∉ S ∪ Q` (here `ϖᵥ ∈ 𝔸_F^∞` is a local uniformiser supported at `v`). Second, there are the Hecke operators `Uᵥ,ₐ` for `v ∈ Q` and `0 ≠ αᵥ ∈ 𝓞ᵥ`, associated the matries `(αᵥ 0; 0 1)`. These slightly nonstandard Hecke operators satisfy `Uᵥ,ₛ * Uᵥ,ₜ = Uᵥ,ₛₜ` and in particular this Hecke algebra is commutative (Hecke operators supported at distinct primes commute because the decomposition of the double cosets into single cosets can be done purely locally).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

