-- L4DEL: intuition: If `φ : 𝔸_K^f ⊗ V → 𝔸_K^f ⊗ V` is `𝔸_K^f`-linear and `φₚ` is its local component at a place `p` then for all `x : 𝔸_K^f ⊗ V` we have `(evalₚ ⊗ id_V) (φ x) = φₚ ((evalₚ ⊗ id_V) x)`, or, more colloquiually, `(φ x)ₚ = φₚ (xₚ)`.
