@file FLT/Deformations/RepresentationTheory/GaloisRep.lean
@decl GaloisRep.HasFlatProlongationAt
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: HasFlatProlongationAt
-- L4DEL: intuition: A galois rep `ρ : Γ K → Aut_A(M)` has a flat prolongation at `v` if `M` (when viewed as a `Γ Kᵥ`) module is isomorphic to the geometric points of a finite etale hopf algebra over `Kᵥ`, and there exists an finite flat hopf algebra over `𝒪ᵥ` whose generic fiber is isomorphic to it. In particular this requires `M` (and by extension `A`) to have finite cardinality. Note that the `Algebra.Etale Kᵥ (Kᵥ ⊗[𝒪ᵥ] G)` condition is redundant because `Kᵥ` has char 0 and all finite flat group schemes over `Kᵥ` are etale. But this would be hard to prove in general, while in the applications they would come from finite groups so it would be easy to show that they are etale. If this turns out to not be the case, we can remove this condition and state the aforementioned result as a sorry.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Deformations/RepresentationTheory/GaloisRep.lean
@decl GaloisRep.IsFlatAt
-- L4DEL: title: A galois rep `ρ : Γ K → Aut_A(M)` is flat at `v` if `A/I ⊗ M` has a flat prolongation at `v` for all open ideals `I`
-- L4DEL: intuition: A galois rep `ρ : Γ K → Aut_A(M)` is flat at `v` if `A/I ⊗ M` has a flat prolongation at `v` for all open ideals `I`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

