@file FLT/Deformations/RepresentationTheory/GaloisRepFamily.lean
@decl GaloisRepFamily.isCompatible
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: isCompatible
-- L4DEL: intuition: A family `ρ_λ` of `E_λ`-adic Galois representations `GaloisRepFamily K E d` of the absolute Galois group of a number field `K` is *compatible* if there is a finite set `S` of finite places of `K` and, for each finite place `v` of `K` not in `S`, a monic degree `d` polynomial `P_v` with coefficients in `E`, such that if `v` and `λ` do not lie above the same rational prime then `ρ_λ` is unramified at `v` and `P_v` is the characteristic polynomial of `ρ_λ(Frob_v)`, where `Frob_v` denotes an arithmetic Frobenius element. This is the weakest possible concept of a compatible family but it will suffice for our needs.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Deformations/RepresentationTheory/IntegralClosure.lean
