@file FLT/KnownIn1980s/EllipticCurves/ReductionBaseChange.lean
@decl ValuativeExtension.(instance at line 186)
-- L4DEL: title: `integerMap` is a local homomorphism: if `integerMap x` is a unit then `x` is a unit
-- L4DEL: intuition: `integerMap` is a local homomorphism: if `integerMap x` is a unit then `x` is a unit. Non-units of the integer subring are exactly the elements of valuation `< 1` (`Valuation.Integer.not_isUnit_iff_valuation_lt_one`), and `valuation k x < 1` gives `valuation l (integerMap k l x) < 1` by `valuation_algebraMap_lt_one`. Needed only to make `IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map` applicable in `residueMap`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/KnownIn1980s/EllipticCurves/ReductionBaseChange.lean
@decl ValuativeExtension.algebraMap_integerMap
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: algebraMap_integerMap
-- L4DEL: intuition: The commuting square `algebraMap 𝒪[l] l ∘ integerMap = algebraMap k l ∘ algebraMap 𝒪[k] k` underlying `integerMap`: on underlying elements both send `x` to `algebraMap k l x` (`integerMap_coe`, and `algebraMap 𝒪[·] ·` is the subring inclusion). This is the functoriality used to transfer integral models along the base change.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/KnownIn1980s/EllipticCurves/ReductionBaseChange.lean
@decl ValuativeExtension.integerMap
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: integerMap
-- L4DEL: intuition: The restriction of `algebraMap k l` to the rings of integers: `𝒪[k]` is the subring `(valuation k).integer` of `k`, and `valuation_algebraMap_le_one` says `algebraMap k l` maps it into `(valuation l).integer`. Implementation note: it may be worth defining the `Algebra 𝒪[k] 𝒪[l]` instance directly instead, so that `WeierstrassCurve.baseChange` (rather than `map`) can be used on integral models in `integralModel_baseChange_map` below; whichever is chosen, this is the underlying ring homomorphism.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/KnownIn1980s/EllipticCurves/ReductionBaseChange.lean
@decl ValuativeExtension.integerMap_coe
-- L4DEL: title: `integerMap` is the algebra map on underlying elements
-- L4DEL: intuition: `integerMap` is the algebra map on underlying elements.
