@file FLT/KnownIn1980s/EllipticCurves/TateCurve.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.qUnitSepClosure
-- L4DEL: title: The image of the Tate parameter in a separable closure `Ω` of `k`, as a unit
-- L4DEL: intuition: The image of the Tate parameter in a separable closure `Ω` of `k`, as a unit. (`Ω` is not a nonarchimedean local field, so this is not literally `(E.baseChange Ω).qUnit`.)
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/KnownIn1980s/EllipticCurves/TateCurve.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.tateA₄
-- L4DEL: title: The coefficient `a₄(q) = -5s₃(q)` of the Tate curve, where `sₖ(q) = ∑_{n≥1} nᵏqⁿ/(1-qⁿ)` (Silverman, ATAEC V.3)
-- L4DEL: intuition: The coefficient `a₄(q) = -5s₃(q)` of the Tate curve, where `sₖ(q) = ∑_{n≥1} nᵏqⁿ/(1-qⁿ)` (Silverman, ATAEC V.3).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/KnownIn1980s/EllipticCurves/TateCurve.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.tateA₄_eq_evalInt
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: tateA₄_eq_evalInt
-- L4DEL: intuition: The Lambert series rearrangement `∑_{n≥1} n³qⁿ/(1-qⁿ) = ∑_{n≥1} σ₃(n)qⁿ` for `|q| < 1`: the defining series of `tateA₄` is the evaluation of the formal series `a₄(q) = -5s₃(q) ∈ ℤ⟦q⟧`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/KnownIn1980s/EllipticCurves/TateCurve.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.tateA₆
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: tateA₆
-- L4DEL: intuition: The coefficient `a₆(q) = -(5s₃(q) + 7s₅(q))/12` of the Tate curve, where `sₖ(q) = ∑_{n≥1} nᵏqⁿ/(1-qⁿ)`; the integrality `12 ∣ 5n³ + 7n⁵` makes sense of the division by `12` in every characteristic (Silverman, ATAEC V.3).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/KnownIn1980s/EllipticCurves/TateCurve.lean
