@decl WeierstrassCurve.weilPairing_tatePoint
-- L4DEL: title: `weilPairing` and `tateEquiv`/`tateEquivSepClosure` are all currently `sorry`ed data, each pinned down mathematically only up to a sign
-- L4DEL: intuition: `weilPairing` and `tateEquiv`/`tateEquivSepClosure` are all currently `sorry`ed data, each pinned down mathematically only up to a sign. The following compatibility, due to Tate, is the demand that these signs be chosen coherently. Note that it constrains the sign convention in the *Weil pairing* (about which the literature does not agree) in terms of the uniformisation, and not vice versa: by bilinearity `e_N(-P, -Q) = e_N(P, Q)`, so the demand is insensitive to negating `tateEquivSepClosure`.
