-- L4DEL: intuition: Evaluation of integral power series commutes with valuative extensions of nonarchimedean local fields: the coefficients are (the same) integers on both sides, and both evaluations are within `|q|^N` of the common `N`-th partial sum (`valuation_evalInt_sub_sum_le`), whose bound transfers along the strictly monotone map of value groups — no continuity argument is needed.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/KnownIn1980s/EllipticCurves/TateCurveBaseChange.lean
@decl TateCurve.hasSum_geometric_succ
-- L4DEL: title: The geometric series over a nonarchimedean local field: for `|x| < 1`, `x + x² + x³ + ⋯ = x/(1 - x)`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The geometric series over a nonarchimedean local field: for `|x| < 1`, `x + x² + x³ + ⋯ = x/(1 - x)`. (Summability is by the nonarchimedean criterion — the terms tend to zero — and the value is identified through the partial sums `x(xⁿ - 1)/(x - 1)`.)
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/KnownIn1980s/EllipticCurves/TateCurveBaseChange.lean
@decl TateCurve.tsum_lambert
-- L4DEL: title: The Lambert series rearrangement over a nonarchimedean local field: for any integer coefficients `c` and `|q| < 1`, `∑_{m≥1} c(m)qᵐ/(1 - qᵐ) = ∑_{N≥1} (∑_{d ∣ N} c(d))qᴺ`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The Lambert series rearrangement over a nonarchimedean local field: for any integer coefficients `c` and `|q| < 1`, `∑_{m≥1} c(m)qᵐ/(1 - qᵐ) = ∑_{N≥1} (∑_{d ∣ N} c(d))qᴺ`. This is the valuative instantiation of the general `tsum_lambert_of_summable` (`FLT.Slop.NumberTheory.TsumDivisorsAntidiagonal`): the geometric row expansions come from `hasSum_geometric_succ`, and the double series is summable since its terms tend to zero nonarchimedeanly (`summable_of_valuation_le_pow`).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/KnownIn1980s/EllipticCurves/TateCurveBaseChange.lean
@decl TateCurve.tsum_lambert_eq_evalInt
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: tsum_lambert_eq_evalInt
-- L4DEL: intuition: Bridge form of the Lambert rearrangement: if the coefficients of `F ∈ ℤ⟦X⟧` are the divisor sums `Fₙ = ∑_{d ∣ n} c(d)`, then the Lambert series of `c` *is* the evaluation of `F` on the open unit disc. This is the form in which `tsum_lambert` is consumed: it turns the defining series of the Tate curve coefficients (`tateA₄`, `tateA₆`) into `evalInt`s in one step.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

