-- L4DEL: intuition: The analytic function `Yₐ(u, q) = ∑_{n : ℤ} (qⁿu)²/(1 - qⁿu)³ + s₁(q)`, defined for `0 < ‖q‖ < 1` and `u ∉ qᶻ` (junk value otherwise). This is the function called `Y(u, q)` in [Silverman, *Advanced topics*, Theorem V.1.1].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

