@file FLT/KnownIn1980s/EllipticCurves/TateParameter.lean
@decl TateCurve.evalInt_mul
-- L4DEL: title: Evaluation of integral power series at a point of the open unit disc is multiplicative
-- L4DEL: intuition: Evaluation of integral power series at a point of the open unit disc is multiplicative. Together with `evalInt_add` this makes `evalInt q` a ring homomorphism `ℤ⟦X⟧ → k` for each `|q| < 1`. Proof: on the open unit disc, `evalInt` is the coercion to `k` of mathlib's topological power-series evaluation over the ring of integers (`key` below): `q` is an integer and topologically nilpotent (`PowerSeries.HasEval`), so `PowerSeries.eval₂Hom` converges in `𝒪[k]` — which is linearly topologized, see the module comment above — and the continuous inclusion `𝒪[k] → k` carries its defining sum (`PowerSeries.hasSum_eval₂`) to the sum defining `evalInt`. Multiplicativity is then `map_mul` of `eval₂Hom`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/KnownIn1980s/EllipticCurves/TateParameter.lean
