@file FLT/Mathlib/Algebra/Algebra/Tower.lean
@decl IsBiscalar
-- L4DEL: title: If `f : A → B` where `A` and `B` are both `R`- and `S`-modules, then `IsBiscalar R S f` asserts that `f` satisfies the linear scalar property for both `R` and `S`
-- L4DEL: intuition: If `f : A → B` where `A` and `B` are both `R`- and `S`-modules, then `IsBiscalar R S f` asserts that `f` satisfies the linear scalar property for both `R` and `S`. I.e., - `f (r • a) = r • f a` - `f (s • a) = s • f a` for all `r : R`, `s : S`, `a : A`. Note that this is symmetric in its arguments and only takes in a function as input. For bundled functions already containing a scalar, this class can be used to assert that the function also has another scalar. The convention in this repo is to use the bundled scalar as the first argument. For example, if `f : A →ₗ[R] B` and it is also scalar with respect to `S`, then use `IsBiscalar R S f`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

