@file FLT/Mathlib/Algebra/IsDirectLimit.lean
@decl IsDirectLimit
-- L4DEL: title: `IsDirectLimit f g` states that `P` is the direct limit of the system `(M i, f i j hij)`
-- L4DEL: intuition: `IsDirectLimit f g` states that `P` is the direct limit of the system `(M i, f i j hij)`. It requires: * `surj`: says every element of `P` comes from some `M i` via the canonical map `g i`. * `inj`: says that if two elements of (possibly different) modules `M i` and `M j` map to the same element of `P`, then they become equal after being mapped into a common later module `M k`. * `compatibility`: ensures that the maps `g i` and `f i j hij` are compatible with one another.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

