@file FLT/Mathlib/Algebra/Polynomial/QuadraticDiscriminant.lean
@decl Polynomial.separable_quadratic_iff
-- L4DEL: title: A quadratic polynomial `a X² + b X + c` (with `a ≠ 0`) over a field is separable exactly when its discriminant `b² - 4 a c` is nonzero
-- L4DEL: intuition: A quadratic polynomial `a X² + b X + c` (with `a ≠ 0`) over a field is separable exactly when its discriminant `b² - 4 a c` is nonzero. The `←` direction holds in every characteristic: by the Bézout identity `sq_derivative_quadratic_sub_mul`, a nonzero (hence invertible) discriminant exhibits `P` and `P'` as coprime. The `→` direction argues that if the discriminant vanishes then `P ∣ (P')²`, forcing the coprimality witness `P` to be a unit, contradicting `deg P = 2`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/Algebra/Polynomial/QuadraticDiscriminant.lean
@decl Polynomial.splits_quadratic_iff
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: splits_quadratic_iff
-- L4DEL: intuition: Over a field of characteristic `≠ 2`, a quadratic `a X² + b X + c` (with `a ≠ 0`) *splits* exactly when its discriminant `b² - 4 a c` is a square: it splits iff it has a root (`splits_quadratic_iff_exists_root`), and completing the square (`discrim_eq_sq_of_quadratic_eq_zero` / `exists_quadratic_eq_zero`) matches roots with square roots of the discriminant. This is the split-multiplicative-reduction criterion; compare `separable_quadratic_iff` (separable ↔ discriminant nonzero).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/Algebra/Polynomial/QuadraticDiscriminant.lean
@decl Polynomial.splits_quadratic_iff_exists_root
-- L4DEL: title: A quadratic `a X² + b X + c` (`a ≠ 0`) over a field splits exactly when it has a root (`Splits.of_natDegree_le_two_of_isRoot`)
-- L4DEL: intuition: A quadratic `a X² + b X + c` (`a ≠ 0`) over a field splits exactly when it has a root (`Splits.of_natDegree_le_two_of_isRoot`). This is the characteristic-free core of the split criterion.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/Algebra/Polynomial/QuadraticDiscriminant.lean
@decl Polynomial.splits_quadratic_iff_of_two_eq_zero
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: splits_quadratic_iff_of_two_eq_zero
-- L4DEL: intuition: Over a field of characteristic `2`, a *separable* quadratic `a X² + b X + c` (`a, b ≠ 0`) splits exactly when its Artin–Schreier invariant `a c / b²` lies in the image of `z ↦ z² + z`, written division-free as `∃ z, b² (z² + z) = a c`. (Substitute `z = a x / b` in a root `x`.) In residue characteristic `2` this replaces the square-class criterion `splits_quadratic_iff`, since there `b² - 4 a c = b²`, so separability already forces `b ≠ 0`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/Algebra/Polynomial/QuadraticDiscriminant.lean
@decl Polynomial.sq_derivative_quadratic_sub_mul
-- L4DEL: title: The Bézout-type identity `(P')² - 4 a · P = C (b² - 4 a c)` for the quadratic `P = a X² + b X + c`: the discriminant is an explicit combination of `P` and its derivative
-- L4DEL: intuition: The Bézout-type identity `(P')² - 4 a · P = C (b² - 4 a c)` for the quadratic `P = a X² + b X + c`: the discriminant is an explicit combination of `P` and its derivative.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

