@file FLT/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/Aut.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.autGroupMulEquiv
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: autGroupMulEquiv
-- L4DEL: intuition: **`Aut(E) ≅ ℤ/2` for `j(E) ∉ {0, 1728}`.** The automorphism group of `E` is `{±1}`, so it is isomorphic to `Multiplicative (ZMod 2)`: it has exactly two elements — `1` and `negVariableChange E` (`eq_one_or_eq_negVariableChange_of_smul_eq`), distinct by `negVariableChange_ne_one`. The isomorphism sends `negVariableChange E` to `Multiplicative.ofAdd 1`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/Aut.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.eq_one_or_eq_negVariableChange_of_smul_eq
-- L4DEL: title: If `j(E) ∉ {0, 1728}` then the only admissible changes of variables fixing `E` are `1` and `negVariableChange E`; that is, `Aut(E) = {±1}`
-- L4DEL: intuition: If `j(E) ∉ {0, 1728}` then the only admissible changes of variables fixing `E` are `1` and `negVariableChange E`; that is, `Aut(E) = {±1}`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/Aut.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.eq_one_or_eq_negVariableChange_of_smul_eq_of_c₄_ne_zero
-- L4DEL: title: If `c₄ ≠ 0` and `c₆ ≠ 0` then the only admissible changes of variables fixing `E` are `1` and `negVariableChange E`
-- L4DEL: intuition: If `c₄ ≠ 0` and `c₆ ≠ 0` then the only admissible changes of variables fixing `E` are `1` and `negVariableChange E`. This is the form of `Aut(E) = {±1}` phrased via `c₄, c₆` (equivalent to `j ∉ {0, 1728}` for an elliptic curve, see `eq_one_or_eq_negVariableChange_of_smul_eq`).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/Aut.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.eq_one_or_eq_negVariableChange_of_u_eq_one
-- L4DEL: title: An automorphism `C` of `E` with `C.u = 1` is either the identity or `negVariableChange E`
-- L4DEL: intuition: An automorphism `C` of `E` with `C.u = 1` is either the identity or `negVariableChange E`. After `r_eq_zero_of_u_eq_one`, the `a₁` and `a₃` laws give `2s = 2t = 0`; in characteristic `≠ 2` this forces `s = t = 0`, and in characteristic `2` the `a₂`, `a₄` laws pin `(s, t)` down to either `(0, 0)` or `(-a₁, -a₃)`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/Aut.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.r_eq_zero_of_u_eq_one
-- L4DEL: title: An automorphism `C` of `E` with `C.u = 1` has no `x`-translation: `C.r = 0`
-- L4DEL: intuition: An automorphism `C` of `E` with `C.u = 1` has no `x`-translation: `C.r = 0`. This follows from the transformation laws of `b₄`, `b₆`, `b₈` together with `c₆ ≠ 0`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/Aut.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.u_eq_one_or_eq_neg_one
-- L4DEL: title: The `u`-coefficient of an automorphism `C` of `E` (with `c₄, c₆ ≠ 0`) satisfies `u² = 1`: the `c₄` and `c₆` laws give `u⁴ = u⁶ = 1`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The `u`-coefficient of an automorphism `C` of `E` (with `c₄, c₆ ≠ 0`) satisfies `u² = 1`: the `c₄` and `c₆` laws give `u⁴ = u⁶ = 1`.
