@file FLT/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/GaloisDescent.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.exists_baseChange_eq_of_map_eq
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: exists_baseChange_eq_of_map_eq
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Galois descent for changes of variables.** A change of variables over `L` fixed by the nontrivial `σ ∈ Gal(L/K)` has all its coefficients in `K`, so it is the base change of a change of variables over `K`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/GaloisDescent.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.exists_baseChange_point_eq_of_map_eq
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: exists_baseChange_point_eq_of_map_eq
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Galois descent for points.** A point of `W(L)` fixed by the nontrivial `σ ∈ Gal(L/K)` (hence, as `[L : K] = 2`, by all of `Gal(L/K)`) is the base change of a point of `W(K)`: its coordinates, being fixed by `σ`, lie in `K`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

