@file FLT/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/Reduction.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.nodePoly_map_splits_iff_isSquare
-- L4DEL: title: Split criterion (residue characteristic ≠ 2).** Over a field `k` of characteristic `≠ 2`, the node polynomial splits — i.e
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Split criterion (residue characteristic ≠ 2).** Over a field `k` of characteristic `≠ 2`, the node polynomial splits — i.e. the two tangent directions at the node are `k`-rational — exactly when its discriminant `-c₄ c₆` (`splitPolynomial_discrim`) is a square in `k`. This is the tool that, applied to a quadratic twist via the scaling `-c₄' c₆' = (t²-4n)⁵ · (-c₄ c₆)`, turns a nonsplit reduction into a split one after twisting by the right square class.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/Reduction.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.nodePoly_map_splits_iff_of_two_eq_zero
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: nodePoly_map_splits_iff_of_two_eq_zero
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Split criterion (residue characteristic 2).** Over a field `k` of characteristic `2`, where the square-class criterion `nodePoly_map_splits_iff_isSquare` fails, the node polynomial splits exactly when its Artin–Schreier invariant lies in the image of `z ↦ z² + z`. Here `c₄` and `c₆` are units, and separability (`b² = -c₄ c₆ ≠ 0`, since `4 = 0`) forces the linear coefficient `a₁ c₄` to be nonzero, so `splits_quadratic_iff_of_two_eq_zero` applies.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/Reduction.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.nodePoly_map_splits_smul_iff
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: nodePoly_map_splits_smul_iff
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Invariance of the node polynomial's splitting under change of variables.** Since a change of variables transforms the node polynomial by an affine substitution and a nonzero scalar (`nodePoly_smul`), whether it splits over a field `k` is unchanged. This is what makes split multiplicative reduction an isomorphism invariant.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/Reduction.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.nodePoly_smul
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: nodePoly_smul
-- L4DEL: intuition: Under a change of variables `C = (u, r, s, t)`, the node polynomial transforms by the affine substitution `T ↦ u T + s` and the unit scalar `u⁻⁶` — reflecting that the tangent slopes `λ` transform as `λ ↦ (λ - s)/u`. In particular its splitting field is unchanged.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

