@file FLT/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/Weierstrass.lean
@decl WeierstrassCurve.splitPolynomial_discrim
-- L4DEL: title: The discriminant of the node's tangent polynomial `c₄ T² + a₁ c₄ T - (54 b₆ - 3 b₂ b₄ + a₂ c₄)` (the quadratic controlling split multiplicative reduction) equals `-c₄ c₆`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The discriminant of the node's tangent polynomial `c₄ T² + a₁ c₄ T - (54 b₆ - 3 b₂ b₄ + a₂ c₄)` (the quadratic controlling split multiplicative reduction) equals `-c₄ c₆`. Hence the tangent directions at the node are rational over the residue field exactly when `-c₄ c₆` is a square there; twisting by `(t, n)` multiplies `-c₄ c₆` by `(t² - 4n)⁵ = (t² - 4n)⁴ · (t² - 4n)`, i.e. by the twisting parameter up to a square (see `c₄_quadraticTwistOf`, `c₆_quadraticTwistOf`).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

