@decl ContinuousCohomology.d_cup_d
-- L4DEL: title: The cup product of two coboundaries is a coboundary: `(d σ) ∪ (d τ) = d (σ ∪ d τ)`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The cup product of two coboundaries is a coboundary: `(d σ) ∪ (d τ) = d (σ ∪ d τ)`. This is the special case of the Leibniz rule `cup_d_comm` where the second argument is a coboundary. Note that `(d σ) ∪ (d τ)` is *not* zero in general: by the Leibniz rule it is the coboundary of `σ ∪ d τ`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

