@file FLT/Mathlib/RepresentationTheory/Homological/ContCohomology/CupProduct.lean
@decl ContRepresentation.cupSucc
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: cupSucc
-- L4DEL: intuition: The inductive step of the cup product: an intertwining map `F : π₁ →ⁱL linHom π₂ π₃` whose underlying pairing `(v, w) ↦ F v w` is jointly continuous induces an intertwining map `π₁.coind₁ →ⁱL linHom π₂ π₃.coind₁` sending `σ` and `τ` to `x ↦ F (σ x) τ`. The joint continuity hypothesis `hF` cannot be dropped: for a general `F` the continuity of `τ ↦ (x ↦ F (σ x) τ)` would require an equicontinuity property of `F` on compact subsets of `C(G, V)`. It is preserved by this construction (`continuous_cupSucc_uncurry`), which allows the construction to be iterated.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/RepresentationTheory/Homological/ContCohomology/CupProduct.lean
@decl ContRepresentation.cupZeroSucc
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: cupZeroSucc
