@file FLT/Mathlib/RingTheory/DiscreteValuationRing/AdjoinRoot.lean
@decl AdjoinRoot.exists_nonZeroDivisor_mul_eq_algebraMap
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: exists_nonZeroDivisor_mul_eq_algebraMap
-- L4DEL: intuition: Clearing denominators in `L = K[X]/(P·K)` over `S = R[X]/(P)`: any element of `L`, multiplied by (the image of) a suitable nonzero element of `R`, lies in the image of `S` (`IsLocalization.integerNormalization` for the polynomial `g` representing the element). The hypothesis `hmap` records that `algebraMap S L` reduces `mk P` to `mk (P·K) ∘ map`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/RingTheory/DiscreteValuationRing/AdjoinRoot.lean
@decl AdjoinRoot.isDiscreteValuationRing_of_irreducible_map_residue
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: isDiscreteValuationRing_of_irreducible_map_residue
-- L4DEL: intuition: For a monic `P` over a discrete valuation ring `R` whose reduction is irreducible over the residue field, `S = R[X]/(P)` is again a discrete valuation ring, *unramified* over `R`: its maximal ideal is `𝔪_R · S` (residue field `(ResidueField R)[X]/(P̄)`), so `R → S` is a local homomorphism.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/RingTheory/DiscreteValuationRing/AdjoinRoot.lean
@decl AdjoinRoot.isFractionRing_map
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: isFractionRing_map
-- L4DEL: intuition: `L = K[X]/(P·K) = Frac(S)` for `S = R[X]/(P)` a discrete valuation ring: `algebraMap S L` is injective (its kernel is a prime of the DVR `S`, and it does not kill a uniformizer), and every element of `L` clears its `K`-denominators (`exists_nonZeroDivisor_mul_eq_algebraMap`) to a multiple in the image of `S`. The hypothesis `hmap` records that `algebraMap S L` reduces `mk P` to `mk (P·K) ∘ map`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/RingTheory/DiscreteValuationRing/AdjoinRoot.lean
@decl AdjoinRoot.isMaximal_map_maximalIdeal
-- L4DEL: title: If the reduction of `P` modulo the maximal ideal of a local ring `A` is irreducible, then `𝔪_A · A[X]/(P)` is a maximal ideal: the quotient by it is the field `(A/𝔪_A)[X]/(P̄)`
-- L4DEL: intuition: If the reduction of `P` modulo the maximal ideal of a local ring `A` is irreducible, then `𝔪_A · A[X]/(P)` is a maximal ideal: the quotient by it is the field `(A/𝔪_A)[X]/(P̄)`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

