@file FLT/Mathlib/RingTheory/Norm/Quadratic.lean
@decl Algebra.IsQuadraticExtension.discrim_ne_zero
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: discrim_ne_zero
-- L4DEL: intuition: If `θ` generates a separable quadratic extension of `K` — that is, lies outside `K` — and `t`, `n` denote its trace and norm, so that `θ² = tθ - n`, then the discriminant `t² - 4n` of the minimal polynomial of `θ` is nonzero. (Over the nontrivial automorphism `σ` it equals `(θ - σθ)²` with `σθ ≠ θ`. In characteristic 2 the statement says `t ≠ 0`: separable quadratic extensions are Artin–Schreier extensions.)
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/RingTheory/Norm/Quadratic.lean
@decl Algebra.IsQuadraticExtension.norm_algebraMap_add_algebraMap_mul
-- L4DEL: title: The norm of `b + aθ` in a separable quadratic extension is `b² + ab·tr(θ) + a²·N(θ)`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The norm of `b + aθ` in a separable quadratic extension is `b² + ab·tr(θ) + a²·N(θ)`.
