@file FLT/Mathlib/RingTheory/Unramified/LocalRing.lean
@decl exists_unramified_extension_of_residueField
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: exists_unramified_extension_of_residueField
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Unramified lifting, arbitrary degree.** A finite separable extension `k'` of the residue field of a discrete valuation ring `R` lifts to an unramified extension `L` of its fraction field `K`: there is a finite separable extension `L/K` with `[L : K] = [k' : k]` and a discrete valuation ring `S` with fraction field `L`, containing `R` via a local homomorphism, whose residue field is `k'`. (The residue degree being `[L : K]` forces ramification index `1`.)
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

