@file FLT/Mathlib/Topology/Algebra/RestrictedProduct/Basic.lean
@decl RestrictedProduct.mapAlongLinearMap
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: mapAlongLinearMap
-- L4DEL: intuition: Given two restricted products `Πʳ (i : ι₁), [R₁ i, B₁ i]_[𝓕₁]` and `Πʳ (j : ι₂), [R₂ j, B₂ j]_[𝓕₂]` of `A`-modules, `RestrictedProduct.mapAlongLinearMap` gives an `A`-linear map between them. The data needed is a function `f : ι₂ → ι₁` such that `𝓕₂` tends to `𝓕₁` along `f`, and `A`-linear maps `φ j : R₁ (f j) → R₂ j` sending `B₁ (f j)` into `B₂ j` for an `𝓕₂`-large set of `j`'s.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

