@file FLT/Mathlib/Topology/Algebra/ValuativeRel/ValuativeTopology.lean
@decl (instance at line 73)
-- L4DEL: title: The ring of integers of a valuative topology is linearly topologized: the open balls `integerBallIdeal` are ideals and form a basis of neighbourhoods of `0`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The ring of integers of a valuative topology is linearly topologized: the open balls `integerBallIdeal` are ideals and form a basis of neighbourhoods of `0`. This is the hypothesis under which mathlib's topological power-series evaluation (`PowerSeries.eval₂Hom`) applies to `𝒪[K]` — it can never apply to the field `K` itself, which has no nontrivial ideals.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Mathlib/Topology/Algebra/ValuativeRel/ValuativeTopology.lean
@decl ValuativeRel.integerBallIdeal
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: integerBallIdeal
-- L4DEL: intuition: The open ball `{x ∈ 𝒪[K] | v(x) < γ}` of the ring of integers is an ideal: ultrametrically it is closed under addition, and multiplying by an integral element only shrinks the valuation.
