@file FLT/Mathlib/Topology/CompactOpen.lean
@decl ContinuousMap.continuous_prodMk
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: continuous_prodMk
-- L4DEL: intuition: The pairing map `C(α, β) × C(α, δ) → C(α, β × δ)` is continuous in the compact-open topologies when `α` is an R₁ space, for instance a topological group, with no assumptions on `β` and `δ`. No local compactness of `α` is required: a compact set mapped into an open set of `β × δ` splits into finitely many compact pieces on each of which both components map into an open rectangle.
