@file FLT/NumberField/AdeleRing.lean
@decl NumberField.AdeleRing.(instance at line 153)
-- L4DEL: title: Take arbitrary `Algebra K L∞`, `Algebra K∞ L∞`, `Algebra 𝔸ᶠ[K] 𝔸ᶠ[L]`, Algebra K 𝔸ᶠ[L]`, `Algebra (𝓞 K) 𝔸ᶠ[L]` and `Algebra (𝔸 K) (𝔸 L)` instances
-- L4DEL: intuition: Take arbitrary `Algebra K L∞`, `Algebra K∞ L∞`, `Algebra 𝔸ᶠ[K] 𝔸ᶠ[L]`, Algebra K 𝔸ᶠ[L]`, `Algebra (𝓞 K) 𝔸ᶠ[L]` and `Algebra (𝔸 K) (𝔸 L)` instances. Assume: - `Algebra K L∞` factors through (existing) `Algebra K L` and `Algebra L L∞`. - `Algebra K∞ L∞` and `Algebra 𝔸ᶠ[K] 𝔸ᶠ[L]` are determined by the fibers of restriction of places of `L` to `K` via (x • y) v = x (v.comap (algebraMap K L)) • y v. - `Algebra K 𝔸ᶠ[L]` factors through (existing) `Algebra K L` and `Algebra L 𝔸ᶠ[L]`. - `Algebra (𝓞 K) 𝔸ᶠ[L]` factors through `Algebra (𝓞 K) (𝓞 L)` and `Algebra (𝓞 L) 𝔸ᶠ[L]`. - `Algebra (𝔸 K) (𝔸 L)` is constructed as the product algebra from `Algebra K∞ L∞` and `Algebra 𝔸ᶠ[K] 𝔸ᶠ[L]. Then the `L` algebra base change map is also linear in `𝔸 K`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

