@decl NumberField.InfiniteAdeleRing.(instance at line 151)
-- L4DEL: title: Take two arbitrary `Algebra K L∞` and `Algebra K∞ L∞` instances
-- L4DEL: intuition: Take two arbitrary `Algebra K L∞` and `Algebra K∞ L∞` instances. Assume that `Algebra K L∞` factors through (existing) `Algebra K L` and `Algebra L L∞`. Assume further that `Algebra K∞ L∞` is determined by the fibers of restriction of infinite places of `L` to `K` via (x • y) v = x (v.comap (algebraMap K L)) • y v. Then the `L` algebra base change map is also linear in `K∞`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

