-- L4DEL: title: If `L/K` and `f : K →+* ℂ`, `g : L →+* ℂ`, then we say `g` is an extension of `f` if `g` restricted to `K` is `f`
-- L4DEL: intuition: If `L/K` and `f : K →+* ℂ`, `g : L →+* ℂ`, then we say `g` is an extension of `f` if `g` restricted to `K` is `f`. This is the complex embedding analogue of `InfinitePlace.Extension`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/NumberField/InfinitePlace/Extension.lean
@decl NumberField.ComplexEmbedding.isExtensionEquivSum
-- L4DEL: title: The extensions `g : L →+* ℂ` of `f : K →+* ℂ` are the direct sum of the mixed and the unmixed extensions
-- L4DEL: intuition: The extensions `g : L →+* ℂ` of `f : K →+* ℂ` are the direct sum of the mixed and the unmixed extensions.
