@file FLT/NumberField/InfinitePlace/Extension.lean
@decl NumberField.ComplexEmbedding.IsMixedExtension
-- L4DEL: title: If `L/K` and `f : K →+* ℂ`, `g : L →+* ℂ`, then `g` is a _mixed extension_ of `f` if the image of `f` is real while the image of `g` is complex
-- L4DEL: intuition: If `L/K` and `f : K →+* ℂ`, `g : L →+* ℂ`, then `g` is a _mixed extension_ of `f` if the image of `f` is real while the image of `g` is complex. This is the complex embedding analogue of `InfinitePlace.RamifiedExtension`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/NumberField/InfinitePlace/Extension.lean
@decl NumberField.ComplexEmbedding.IsUnmixedExtension
-- L4DEL: title: If `L/K` and `f : K →+* ℂ`, `g : L →+* ℂ`, then `g` is an _unmixed extension_ of `f` if `g` is an extension of `f` but is not a mixed extension
-- L4DEL: intuition: If `L/K` and `f : K →+* ℂ`, `g : L →+* ℂ`, then `g` is an _unmixed extension_ of `f` if `g` is an extension of `f` but is not a mixed extension. In other words, the image of `f` is real if and only if the image of `g` is real. This is the complex embedding analogue of `InfinitePlace.UnramifiedExtension`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/NumberField/InfinitePlace/Extension.lean
