@file FLT/QuaternionAlgebra/NumberField.lean
@decl IsQuaternionAlgebra.NumberField.IsUnramified
-- L4DEL: title: A quaternion algebra over a number field is unramified if it is split at all finite places
-- L4DEL: intuition: A quaternion algebra over a number field is unramified if it is split at all finite places. This is implemented as the existence of a rigidification of `D`, that is, an isomorphism `D ⊗[F] 𝔸_F^∞ = M₂(𝔸_F^∞)`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/QuaternionAlgebra/NumberField.lean
@decl IsQuaternionAlgebra.NumberField.WithRigidification
-- L4DEL: title: A rigidification of a quaternion algebra D over a number field F is a fixed choice of `𝔸_F^∞`-algebra isomorphism `D ⊗[F] 𝔸_F^∞ = M₂(𝔸_F^∞)`
-- L4DEL: intuition: A rigidification of a quaternion algebra D over a number field F is a fixed choice of `𝔸_F^∞`-algebra isomorphism `D ⊗[F] 𝔸_F^∞ = M₂(𝔸_F^∞)`. In other words, it is a choice of splitting of `D ⊗[F] Fᵥ` (i.e. an isomorphism to `M₂(Fᵥ)`) for all finite places `v` together with a guarantee that the isomorphism works on the integral level at all but finitely many places. Such a rigidification exists if and only if F is unramified at all finite places.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/QuaternionAlgebra/NumberField.lean
