@file FLT/Slop/DimensionTheorem/Numeric.lean
@decl DimensionTheorem.GrowthLE.telescope_aux
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: telescope_aux
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Telescoping lemma.** If `g` is monotone and, for `n ≥ c`, the value `g n` is dominated by the difference `f n - f (n - c)` (stated additively as `g n + f (n - c) ≤ f n`), and `f` has growth degree at most `d + 1`, then `g` has growth degree at most `d`. This is the numerical heart of the inductive step `dim ≤ d(R)` in the dimension theorem: passing to `R/xR` drops the growth degree of the Hilbert–Samuel function.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

