@decl DimensionTheorem.multichoose_le_pow
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: multichoose_le_pow
-- L4DEL: intuition: The number of monomials of degree `n` in `k` variables is at most `(n + 1) ^ (k - 1)` (for `k ≥ 1`): a multiset of size `n` over `Fin k` is determined by the multiplicities of the first `k - 1` elements, each of which lies in `{0, ..., n}`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FLT/Slop/NumberTheory/TsumDivisorsAntidiagonal.lean
@decl (example at line 114)
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: (example at line 114)
-- L4DEL: intuition: `hgeo → IsTopologicallyNilpotent r`: the row hypothesis is strictly stronger than topological nilpotency, which is why the completeness-based companion below can take the weaker `IsTopologicallyNilpotent r` in its place. Only the first row `hgeo 1` is needed — a `HasSum` family is null along the cofinite filter (`= atTop` on `ℕ`), i.e. `rⁿ → 0`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own leading source comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

